@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# @olonjs/core
+
+> The Sovereign Core Engine for [OlonJS](https://olon.js.org) — websites that are natively readable and operable by AI agents.
+
+[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@olonjs/core?color=blue&style=flat-square)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@olonjs/core)
+[![license](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green?style=flat-square)](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/LICENSE)
+
+OlonJS is the AI-native content infrastructure for the agentic web. Every page is a typed JSON contract served at `/{slug}.json`, validated with Zod, and exposed to agents through a per-tenant MCP gateway with scope-bound OAuth. No scraping. No guesswork. One deterministic surface for humans and agents.
+
+`@olonjs/core` is the runtime engine that powers it: routing, state orchestration, schema validation, and deterministic rendering.
+
+---
+
+## Quickstart
+
+You do not install `@olonjs/core` directly. You scaffold a tenant with the CLI, which wires the core in for you.
+
+```bash
+npx @olonjs/cli new tenant my-agentic-site --template alpha
+cd my-agentic-site
+npm run dev
+```
+
+Then verify the agent surface:
+
+```bash
+# Human view
+curl http://localhost:5173/
+
+# Agent view — the typed contract for the same page
+curl http://localhost:5173/home.json
+```
+
+You should see a Zod-validated JSON document describing the page's sections, ready to be consumed by any MCP-aware agent.
+
+---
+
+## What you get
+
+- **Typed JSON contracts.** Every route ships a `/{slug}.json` sidecar. The schema is the API.
+- **WebMCP-ready.** OlonJS tenants act as MCP servers: pages are Resources, sections are Tools.
+- **Deterministic rendering.** The same contract produces the same DOM. No surprises for agents or for humans.
+- **Sovereign by design.** Your tenant, your schema, your data. Git-backed, self-hostable, MIT-licensed.
+
+## When to reach for OlonJS
+
+- You are building an AI product that needs to read or operate websites reliably.
+- You publish content and want agents to consume it without HTML scraping.
+- You want to expose scoped, OAuth-gated actions to AI agents without writing a custom MCP server.
+
+## Documentation
+
+- [Architecture](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)
+- [CLI reference](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/docs/CLI.md)
+- [WebMCP browser API](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/docs/webmcp.md)
+- [Canonical schemas](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/docs/canonical-schemas-howto.md)
+- [Spec v1.6](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/specs/olonjsSpecs_V_1_6.md)
+
+## Ecosystem
+
+| Package | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| [`@olonjs/cli`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@olonjs/cli) | Tenant generator. Your entry point. |
+| [`@olonjs/core`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@olonjs/core) | Runtime engine. This package. |
+| [`@olonjs/stack`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@olonjs/stack) | Dependency manifest for tenants. |
+| [`@olonjs/mcp`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@olonjs/mcp) | Local MCP server bridge for Zero-UI automation. |
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Node.js 18+
+- React 19, React DOM 19, React Router 6.29+, Zod 3.24+ (peer dependencies)
+
+## License
+
+MIT © OlonJS Team. See [LICENSE](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/LICENSE).
+
+— Built in Italy. Learn more at [olon.js.org](https://olon.js.org).
