+# @olonjs/mcp
+
+> Local MCP server bridge for [OlonJS](https://olon.js.org) tenants. Enables Zero-UI automation of an OlonJS site via Playwright, exposed as MCP tools.
+
+[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@olonjs/mcp?color=blue&style=flat-square)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@olonjs/mcp)
+[![license](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green?style=flat-square)](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/LICENSE)
+
+`@olonjs/mcp` runs locally and bridges your AI editor or agent runtime to a running OlonJS tenant. It exposes each section of every page as an MCP Tool, and each typed JSON contract as an MCP Resource, so an agent can read pages and trigger scoped mutations through a clean tool surface.
+
+## Quickstart
+
+If you scaffolded a tenant with `@olonjs/cli`, configure your editor in one command:
+
+```bash
+npx @olonjs/cli init-mcp
+```
+
+That writes the right entry into Cursor / Cline / compatible MCP clients, pointing them at `npx -y @olonjs/mcp@latest http://localhost:5174`.
+
+To run it manually against any OlonJS tenant:
+
+```bash
+npx -y @olonjs/mcp@latest http://localhost:5173
+```
+
+## What it exposes
+
+- **Resources** — every `/{slug}.json` typed contract on the tenant.
+- **Tools** — Playwright-driven actions for each section type, scoped to the tenant's schema.
+- **Health checks** — verify the WebMCP surface is ready before invoking tools.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- A running OlonJS tenant (`npm run dev` inside the tenant directory).
+- Node.js 18+.
+- Playwright browsers (installed on first run).
+
+## Documentation
+
+- [WebMCP browser API](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/docs/webmcp.md)
+- [MCP guide](https://github.com/olonjs/npm-jpcore/blob/main/docs/mcp-guide.md)
+
+## License
+
+MIT © OlonJS Team.
+
+— Learn more at [olon.js.org](https://olon.js.org).
